On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:02:33 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> This failed to build. You can find the logs at https://poudriere.p7x.dev

Thanks for running it. The build is 150-local 2026-10-15_00h44m26s,
and it failed in extract:

    ===> Fetching all distfiles required by signoz-0.145.0 for building
    rm: go.mod: Permission denied
    *** Error code 1

Every phase after fetch runs the fetch target again, and poudriere runs
extract as nobody, offline, with DISTFILES owned by root. The port's
post-fetch removed and rewrote go.mod in DIST_SUBDIR each time it ran,
so the second run could not. My earlier builds all ran as the owner
of DISTDIR, which is why they missed it. v3 has the same fault, since
it changed only the vendor patch header.

The fix is posted as "[freebsd-ports PATCH v4] net-mgmt/signoz:
Observability platform for logs, metrics, and traces" [1]. post-fetch
now prints the edited go.mod with "go mod edit -print" and replaces
the file only when it differs, so fetch writes it once and extract
only reads it. devel/gitlab-runner guards its own write into
DIST_SUBDIR the same way.

To test it, I copied poudriere's conditions as far as I can without
root. I fetched into a fresh DISTDIR, then made it read-only and cut
the network by pointing HTTP_PROXY and HTTPS_PROXY at a closed port.
Under those conditions v3 fails with the same "rm: go.mod: Permission
denied", and v4 passes extract, build, stage, and check-plist.
portclippy, portfmt, and portlint are clean. A real poudriere run is
still the check that counts.

One note on the logs: poudriere.p7x.dev has no public DNS record, and
this jail resolves through 8.8.8.8, so the name did not resolve. I
reached the server at 10.20.0.3, its address in
doc/notes/home-network.org.

